 who has out-raised Bankhead", "Prediction markets price Democratic chances near zero"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Republican Kurt Alme ahead by 20 or more points, and all ten expert ratings put the race at Safe or Solid R. The Democratic nominee's weak fundraising and the presence of a well-funded independent pulling anti-Alme votes make a Democratic win implausible.", "watch": "A late consolidation of anti-Alme voters behind one challenger, or a major outside-spending surge, could narrow the margin without changing the likely outcome.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Steve Daines (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Montana's open Senate seat, left vacant by Steve Daines' retirement, is expected to remain in Republican hands. Kurt Alme has built a clear financial and polling advantage, leading recent surveys by roughly 20 to 25 points in a state that leans Republican by about ten points. The U.S. Chamber of Commerce has endorsed him, and outside groups are active on his side.\n\nThe anti-Alme vote is divided between Democrat Alani Bankhead, who has raised under $60,000, and independent Seth Bodnar, who has out-raised both major-party nominees but trails Alme in polls. Bankhead declined to withdraw at the filing deadline despite pressure, and Planned Parenthood endorsed the independent instead. Prediction markets give Democrats about a one percent chance, and expert raters unanimously place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0053, "margin": -15.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0066, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0028, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.004, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0021, "margin": -20.0}]}